<article class="env-remark" id="07MS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07MS">Remark <span data-tag="07MS">60.24.8</span> <span class="named">(Base change map)</span>.</a>  In the situation of Remark <a href="/tag/07MJ" data-tag="07MJ">60.24.1</a> assume $S = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ and $S' = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A')$ are affine. Let $\mathcal{F}'$ be an $\mathcal{O}_{X'/S'}$-module. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be the pullback of $\mathcal{F}'$. Then there is a canonical base change map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  L(S' \to S)^*R\tau _{X'/S', *}\mathcal{F}' \longrightarrow R\tau _{X/S, *}\mathcal{F}  \]
</div>
  <p> where $\tau _{X/S}$ and $\tau _{X'/S'}$ are the structure morphisms, see Remark <a href="/tag/07IM" data-tag="07IM">60.9.6</a>. On global sections this gives a base change map </p>
  <div class="equation" id="07MT">
    <span class="equation-label"><a href="/tag/07MT" data-tag="07MT">60.24.8.1</a></span>
  <div>\begin{equation}  \label{crystalline-equation-base-change-map} R\Gamma (\text{Cris}(X'/S'), \mathcal{F}') \otimes ^\mathbf {L}_{A'} A \longrightarrow R\Gamma (\text{Cris}(X/S), \mathcal{F}) \end{equation}</div>
</div>
  <p> in $D(A)$. </p>
  <p>Hint: Compose the very general base change map of Cohomology on Sites, Remark <a href="/tag/07A7" data-tag="07A7">21.19.3</a> with the canonical map $Lf_{\text{cris}}^*\mathcal{F}' \to f_{\text{cris}}^*\mathcal{F}' = \mathcal{F}$. </p>
</article>